32	/**
33	 * Utility that can be used to map values from a supplied source to a destination.
34	 * Primarily intended to be help when mapping from
35	 * {@link ConfigurationProperties @ConfigurationProperties} to third-party classes.
36	 * <p>
37	 * Can filter values based on predicates and adapt values if needed. For example:
38	 * <pre class="code">
39	 * PropertyMapper map = PropertyMapper.get();
40	 * map.from(source::getName)
41	 *   .to(destination::setName);
42	 * map.from(source::getTimeout)
43	 *   .when(this::thisYear)
44	 *   .asInt(Duration::getSeconds)
45	 *   .to(destination::setTimeoutSecs);
46	 * map.from(source::isEnabled)
47	 *   .whenFalse().
48	 *   .toCall(destination::disable);
49	 * </pre>
50	 * <p>
51	 * Mappings can ultimately be applied to a {@link Source#to(Consumer) setter}, trigger a
52	 * {@link Source#toCall(Runnable) method call} or create a
53	 * {@link Source#toInstance(Function) new instance}.
54	 * <p>
55	 * By default {@code null} values and any {@link NullPointerException} thrown from the
56	 * supplier are filtered and will not be applied to consumers. If you want to apply nulls,
57	 * you can use {@link Source#always()}.
58	 *
59	 * @author Phillip Webb
60	 * @author Artsiom Yudovin
61	 * @author Chris Bono
62	 * @author Moritz Halbritter
63	 * @since 2.0.0
64	 */
